{"name":"Bologna","hex":"#9c6f6c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bologna","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A province of Emilia-Romagna, Italy.","The capital city of Emilia-Romagna, Italy, the capital of Bologna and also of Emilia-Romagna."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bologna"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bologna","blocks":[{"text":"Bologna is the capital and largest city of the Emilia-Romagna region in northern Italy. It is the seventh most populous city in Italy, with 391,473 inhabitants from 150 different nationalities. Its metropolitan province is home to more than 1 million people as of 2026. Bologna is most famous for being the home to the oldest university in continuous operation, the University of Bologna, established in AD 1088."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Torri_di_Bologna%2C_Bologna.jpg/330px-Torri_di_Bologna%2C_Bologna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bologna","wikidata":"Q1891"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Basilica_di_San_Luca.._Bologna.jpg/500px-Basilica_di_San_Luca.._Bologna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Basilica_di_San_Luca.._Bologna.jpg/500px-Basilica_di_San_Luca.._Bologna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABasilica_di_San_Luca.._Bologna.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Bologna_fontana_del_Nettuno_07feb08_03.jpg/500px-Bologna_fontana_del_Nettuno_07feb08_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Bologna_fontana_del_Nettuno_07feb08_03.jpg/1280px-Bologna_fontana_del_Nettuno_07feb08_03.jpg?ut